{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837988",
      "title": "Validating Input Upon Lost Focus (Blur)",
      "sourceHash": "dc5883563d0b0be978352da0728aa7878f8deb21c174b9126a896c60b8ec5bcd",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 3.03,
          "en": "So how can we validate inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.03,
          "end": 6.09,
          "en": "on lost focus?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.09,
          "end": 8.16,
          "en": "Well, for that, we need to react",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.16,
          "end": 10.71,
          "en": "to an input field losing focus.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.71,
          "end": 14.19,
          "en": "For example, the email input field again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.19,
          "end": 18.33,
          "en": "And you can react to this input losing focus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.33,
          "end": 22.41,
          "en": "by adding another event listening Prop to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.41,
          "end": 24.39,
          "en": "the onBlur Prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.39,
          "end": 29.39,
          "en": "because the blur event is a built-in default browser event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.64,
          "end": 34.583,
          "en": "that will be fired whenever this input loses focus.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36,
          "end": 40.41,
          "en": "Therefore, we can add a new event handling function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.41,
          "end": 41.26,
          "en": "handleEmailBlur",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.25,
          "end": 48.16,
          "en": "or of course, set up a more generic handleInputBlur",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 51.66,
          "end": 53.85,
          "en": "event handling function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.85,
          "end": 58.85,
          "en": "And then here, we could again accept an identifier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 59.04,
          "end": 59.883,
          "en": "like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.87,
          "end": 63.93,
          "en": "and manage a new piece of state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 63.93,
          "end": 67.62,
          "en": "Because now, we don't just wanna keep track of the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 67.62,
          "end": 69.9,
          "en": "that has been entered into an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.9,
          "end": 71.67,
          "en": "but we also wanna keep track",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.67,
          "end": 76.35,
          "en": "of whether the user touched this value or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.35,
          "end": 78.78,
          "en": "Because when the blur event is fired",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.78,
          "end": 83.03999999999999,
          "en": "and this input field therefore loses focus,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 83.03999999999999,
          "end": 87.45,
          "en": "we of course, also know that it seemed to have focus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.45,
          "end": 89.1,
          "en": "in the first place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 89.1,
          "end": 91.74,
          "en": "So that the user did touch it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.74,
          "end": 93.87299999999999,
          "en": "that the user worked with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.97999999999999,
          "end": 97.86,
          "en": "Hence, we need that second piece of state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.86,
          "end": 99.12,
          "en": "or we could of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.12,
          "end": 101.64,
          "en": "also merge it into this existing state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.64,
          "end": 105.75,
          "en": "by managing some nested object here for the email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.75,
          "end": 110.13,
          "en": "where we have the value and the didBlur",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.13,
          "end": 113.64,
          "en": "or didEdit property which initially is false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.64,
          "end": 116.00999999999999,
          "en": "and then might be set to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 116.00999999999999,
          "end": 119.97,
          "en": "But here, I'll simply go for an extra piece of state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.97,
          "end": 120.963,
          "en": "with useState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.52,
          "end": 125.1,
          "en": "And then again, I'll manage an object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.1,
          "end": 128.4,
          "en": "with an email property which initially is false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 132.27,
          "en": "And the password property, which initially is false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.27,
          "end": 136.66,
          "en": "because this here will be my didEdit state and set didEdit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.55,
          "end": 142.38,
          "en": "where I keep track of whether these inputs have been edited.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 142.38,
          "end": 147.38,
          "en": "Which in my case here, simply means that they lost focus.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 147.39,
          "end": 152.073,
          "en": "So the user interacted with them and then they lost focus.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 153.45,
          "end": 156.21,
          "en": "Therefore, now with that state added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 158.43,
          "en": "here in handleInputBlur,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 158.43,
          "end": 162.66,
          "en": "I wanna update this didEdit state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 162.66,
          "end": 166.71,
          "en": "by again, using the function form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 166.71,
          "end": 168.99,
          "en": "where I return a new object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 168.99,
          "end": 171.24,
          "en": "where I spread in my old state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 171.24,
          "end": 175.29,
          "en": "so that we don't lose any data and information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 175.29,
          "end": 179.64,
          "en": "And then just as with the handleInputChange function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 179.64,
          "end": 184.44,
          "en": "will dynamically target a property with this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 184.44,
          "end": 187.33,
          "en": "And then here, simply set it to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 188.25,
          "end": 191.88,
          "en": "because this will be fired when an input is blurred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 191.88,
          "end": 195.153,
          "en": "So therefore, then I wanna set this state to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 196.07999999999998,
          "end": 199.413,
          "en": "Keep in mind that initially, it is false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 201.78,
          "end": 204.75,
          "en": "And the offer now it's handleInputBlur,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 204.75,
          "end": 206.64,
          "en": "which I wanna trigger here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 206.64,
          "end": 209.13,
          "en": "And again, we need to wrap this with a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 209.13,
          "end": 212.19,
          "en": "so that we can control how it will be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 212.19,
          "end": 217.19,
          "en": "so that we can pass this identifier to handleInputBlur.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 217.32,
          "end": 220.473,
          "en": "In this case, email as an identifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 222.18,
          "end": 225.57,
          "en": "And now, we can use this new didEdit state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 225.57,
          "end": 228.15,
          "en": "to perform validation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 228.15,
          "end": 231.48,
          "en": "And we can check whether emailIsInvalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 231.48,
          "end": 236.48,
          "en": "by not checking for whether it still has the initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 236.91,
          "end": 241.74,
          "en": "but by instead keeping this check and combining this check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 241.74,
          "end": 244.233,
          "en": "with didEdit.email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 245.61,
          "end": 249.03,
          "en": "If the user did edit the email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 249.03,
          "end": 253.23,
          "en": "and the email then does not include an @ symbol,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 253.23,
          "end": 256.413,
          "en": "I want to set emailIsInvalid as true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 257.55,
          "end": 259.47,
          "en": "And with that, we make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 259.47,
          "end": 262.62,
          "en": "that we give the user a chance of editing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 262.62,
          "end": 264.873,
          "en": "before we run this check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 266.19,
          "end": 269.073,
          "en": "And therefore, before we show an error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 270.24,
          "end": 273.78,
          "en": "So with that, if you save this all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 273.78,
          "end": 275.79,
          "en": "and you go back and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 275.79,
          "end": 279.063,
          "en": "you see there's no error message here initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 280.14,
          "end": 283.563,
          "en": "And if I start typing, there still is no error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 284.4,
          "end": 288.36,
          "en": "But if I then type out of there and I lose focus,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 288.36,
          "end": 290.373,
          "en": "there is an error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 291.42,
          "end": 294.48,
          "en": "And I also get that if I just click in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 294.48,
          "end": 297.093,
          "en": "don't enter anything, and click out of here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 298.47,
          "end": 300.36,
          "en": "As soon as I start typing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 300.36,
          "end": 303.993,
          "en": "the error goes away once I have a valid value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 304.86,
          "end": 309.63,
          "en": "And that's now arguably a good user experience, therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 309.63,
          "end": 311.64,
          "en": "Now on the slide I mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 311.64,
          "end": 315.15,
          "en": "that when validating on lost focus,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 315.15,
          "end": 318.96,
          "en": "errors may be shown too long though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 318.96,
          "end": 320.883,
          "en": "And what do I mean by that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 322.08,
          "end": 324.33,
          "en": "Well, here, you could argue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 324.33,
          "end": 328.2,
          "en": "that the error is shown a little bit too long",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 328.2,
          "end": 330.72,
          "en": "because if I have that error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 330.72,
          "end": 332.64,
          "en": "and I start typing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 332.64,
          "end": 337.64,
          "en": "it only disappears once we did enter a valid value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 337.77,
          "end": 339.72,
          "en": "Which you could argue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 339.72,
          "end": 342.33299999999997,
          "en": "is the experience you might wanna provide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 343.38,
          "end": 345.18,
          "en": "But you could also argue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 345.18,
          "end": 348.65999999999997,
          "en": "that this error message should disappear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 348.65999999999997,
          "end": 352.86,
          "en": "as soon as the user starts typing again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 352.86,
          "end": 355.98,
          "en": "Because once the user starts typing again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 355.98,
          "end": 359.79,
          "en": "they have another chance of entering a valid value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 359.79,
          "end": 363.45,
          "en": "and therefore, we might wanna remove this error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 363.45,
          "end": 368.45,
          "en": "until they're done typing and the input loses focus again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 368.82,
          "end": 370.05,
          "en": "at which point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 370.05,
          "end": 372.603,
          "en": "we might wanna run this validation again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 374.01,
          "end": 376.83,
          "en": "And therefore, the solution we have at the moment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 376.83,
          "end": 378.33,
          "en": "could be improved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 378.33,
          "end": 382.08,
          "en": "by also updating didEdit on every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 382.08,
          "end": 384.33,
          "en": "And by resetting this to false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 384.33,
          "end": 386.913,
          "en": "whenever the user starts typing again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 387.87,
          "end": 390.52,
          "en": "And we can do this by going to handleInputChange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 391.74,
          "end": 395.013,
          "en": "and also updating setDidEdit here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 396.06,
          "end": 398.88,
          "en": "And again here, we would use the function form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 398.88,
          "end": 400.95,
          "en": "for updating this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 400.95,
          "end": 404.34000000000003,
          "en": "and copy in the old state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 404.34000000000003,
          "end": 407.22,
          "en": "and then target and input dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 407.22,
          "end": 412.2,
          "en": "via its identifier to reset it to false here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 412.2,
          "end": 414.99,
          "en": "So that whenever the user starts typing again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 414.99,
          "end": 417.45,
          "en": "we reset this didEdit state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 417.45,
          "end": 420.933,
          "en": "for the input in which the user types again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 422.73,
          "end": 425.91,
          "en": "And with that, you'll see there's no error initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 425.91,
          "end": 428.49,
          "en": "but we do get one if I lose focus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 428.49,
          "end": 431.55,
          "en": "and have an invalid value in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 431.55,
          "end": 433.71,
          "en": "But if I then start typing again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 433.71,
          "end": 436.32,
          "en": "the error is removed again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 436.32,
          "end": 438.45,
          "en": "and it reappears if I,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 438.45,
          "end": 442.8,
          "en": "again, lose focus without a valid value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 442.8,
          "end": 446.61,
          "en": "And therefore, this might then be the best of both worlds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 446.61,
          "end": 450.78,
          "en": "And indeed, combining validation on every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 450.78,
          "end": 453.81,
          "en": "with validation on lost focus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 453.81,
          "end": 456.48,
          "en": "and resetting that focus state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 456.48,
          "end": 458.97,
          "en": "whenever the user starts typing again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 458.97,
          "end": 462.933,
          "en": "can be a good pattern for validating user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 463.89,
          "end": 468,
          "en": "But it's not the only way of validating input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
